From 6f7559e5c255d873cbb5a37b511b17fb638ab75e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:00:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] stream-mmq: the streamed experts through llama.cpp's MMQ, the
 MXFP4 bytes regrouped on the GPU

The streamed prefill dequantized each group of MXFP4 experts to bf16 and ran
the bf16 CUTLASS MoE (W16). At the windows the prefill plan picks that is
GEMM-bound: a layer took 38 ms plus 12 ms a thousand rows on each of two
RTX 5070 Ti, above the 159 ms the PCIe link needs for the layer's 3.6 GB.

With KT_GPU_STREAM_MMQ=1 each group's MXFP4 bytes are regrouped on the GPU
into ggml block_mxfp4 (one Triton kernel: the E8M0 byte of kt-kernel's fp32
power-of-two scale, then values j and j + 16 in one byte) and multiplied by
llama.cpp's MMQ (kt_gguf_moe_mmq, the GGUF recipe's extension, which gains
the MXFP4 type): int8 mma on the activations and the clamped SwiGLU
intermediate quantized per 32 values with an fp16 scale. The weights stay
exact. The routes are sorted by expert once a layer (one host sync); a
group's slot goes back to the DMA as soon as it is regrouped. Neither the
bf16 MoE output nor the CUTLASS workspace is allocated, so the plan's
windows can grow. Ranks whose rows come from several kt-kernel parts (one
GPU over two NUMA nodes) regroup part by part.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017, the MXFP4 recipe (two RTX 5070 Ti, two EPYC 7452):
- A layer at 12,288 rows: 154-168 ms (182-192 with W16), now the PCIe time.
  At 35,000 rows the MoE math alone is 107 ms (462 with W16).
- 24-piece NLL with every piece through the streamer (threshold 256, fixed
  hot slots): reference + 0.0005 (W16) and - 0.0004 (MMQ), MMQ - W16
  -0.0009 (SE 0.0033); on one GPU +0.0034 and -0.0013, -0.0047 (SE 0.0044).
  Greedy answers identical to W16.
- With the plan's cost a row at 300 KiB (serve.sh): 35K prefill 1,806 tok/s
  (1,290 with W16 at the old 460 KiB), 131K 1,881 (1,452), 1M 1,087
  (941-943); one GPU 35K 1,056 (862), 65K 1,154 (811). No OOM, no
  allocator retries.

llama.cpp's ggml/ (33 files of 23b0202, 17,130 lines) is not carried here: the recipe's
lib/llama-mmq.sh fetches them, applies its patches/llama-mmq.patch (the 15 changed files and the IQ1_M
instance) and checks every file against patches/llama-mmq.sha256, so the extension builds from the same bytes.

Prerequisites: stream-prefill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GYXChrDp1ydY24uuGvf2k2
